No worries.

> Is there a way to plot multiple predictions on the same graph and use color/line-style to differentiate them?

Yup:

    preds1 = ezPredict(...)
    preds2 = ezPredict(...)
    preds_both = list(
        cells = rbind(
            cbind(
                preds1$cells
                , version = '1'
            )
            , cbind(
                preds2$cells
                , version = '2'
            )
        )
        boots = rbind(
            cbind(
                preds1$boots
                , version = '1'
            )
            , cbind(
                preds2$boots
                , version = '2'
            )
        )
    )
    ezPlot2(
        preds = preds_both
        , x = ...
        , split = version
    )

